> This recipe is for the baseline form, read the variants below and decide what you want accordingly.

Melt @butter{4%tbsp}(unsalted, melted then cooled) and add @vegetable oil{4%tbsp} to bring it all down to room temperature.

In a large mixing bowl, combine @buttermilk{1%cup}(room temperature, can sub yogurt or sour cream in equal amount), @eggs{2%large}(room temperature), @sugar{3/4%cup}, @baking powder{2%tsp}, @baking soda{1/2%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}. 

Add vanilla or other extracts, if using. 

Whisk together until sugar mostly dissolves. 

Whisk in the butter and oil combo.

Fold in @all purpose flour{2.25%cups} just until the last of it disappears. If adding any mix-ins, do so at the point when some flour is still visible. This avoids over-mixing which can lead to tough muffins.

Use a medium scoop, or a couple spoons, to distribute the muffin batter into each of the prepared muffin pan wells. Top with sparkling sugar or streusel if desired.

Bake at 425°F for ~{5%minutes}, then drop the temperature to 350°F, without opening the oven. Bake for another ~{18-22%minutes}, or until a toothpick or skewer inserted into the center of a muffin comes out clean or with just a few crumbs.

Let cool for ~{5%minutes} in the muffin pan and then carefully transfer to a #wire rack{} to cool for at least ~{15%minutes} longer. Although you have removed them from the oven, they will continue to cook from their own residual heat for a few minutes. Open one up too soon and they will crumble. Give them a minute to get it together.

== Cinnamon Streusel ==
> Inspired by: https://brokenovenbaking.com/cinnamon-streusel-muffins/

Mix 2.67 tbsp unsalted butter, melted, .5 cup all-purpose flour, .25 cup light brown sugar, and .5 tbsp ground cinnamon. When pouring in the batter, follow the order: 1 tsp streusel -> 1 tbsp batter -> 2 tsp streusel -> fill to 3/4 with batter -> top with streusel.

== Jammy Swirl ==
Distribute 1/2 cup jam across all uncooked muffins, while they're still in the tin. Using a toothpick or skewer to mix in.

== Fruit Muffins ==
To make i.e. blueberry muffins, toss 1.5 cup whole or chopped fruit in the finished batter. Top with streusel or coarse sugar and bake as directed.

== Chocolate Chip ==
Fold 1.5 cups chocolate chips into the finished batter, before distributing to the tin. Top with more chips as desired.

== Lemon Poppy Seed ==
Rub lemon zest into sugar with your fingers. Add 2 tablespoons of poppy seeds to the wet ingredients. Add 1 teaspoon lemon extract, if desired. Top with streusel or a lemon glaze made of 1 cup confectioners sugar and 1-2 tablespoons of lemon juice to drizzle or dip. Bake as directed.

== Double Chocolate ==
Replace all-purpose flour with 1.5 cups all purpose flour and 1/2 cup of cocoa powder. Add 1 cup of chocolate chips. Put some more chips on top before baking. Bake as directed. 

== Banana ==
Replace half of your buttermilk with 2 mashed bananas and mix into wet ingredients. Toss in 1/2 cup of toasted walnuts or pecans if you'd like, and top with streusel. Bake as directed.

== Apple Cinnamon Crunch ==
Add 1.5 teaspoons of ground cinnamon to dry ingredients. Fold in .75 - 1 cup of diced apples that have been sauteed for 3-4 minutes in 2 tablespoons of butter. Scoop into muffin tin and sprinkle with coarse sugar. Bake as directed.

== Raspberry Banana ==
Replace half of your buttermilk with 2 mashed bananas and fold in 2 cups of raspberries (frozen for 15 to 30 minutes so they won't break apart). Sprinkle with coarse sugar and bake as directed.